A1. This makes a good start and was the best bet of the new deal. ~ ALPHA
A6. Collapsible and built of wooden promises. ~ PLATFORM
A13. Filibuster phenagling. ~ DELAY
A14. "Looky! Looky! Looky!" ~ OBSERVE
A16. Master of Ceremonies (abbr.). ~ MC
A17. A political sentence. ~ TERM
A19. Malay canoe. ~ PROA
A20. Give it a rah for Borah. ~ BO
A21. Third party in possession. ~ ITS
A23. This will run in the spring. ~ SAP
A24. A work measure for the platform. ~ ERG
A25. If this is on the platform, it will cause a revolution. ~ FAN
A26. Crank cases. ~ NUTS
A28. A city that didn't get it. ~ CY
A29. Conniptions. ~ FITS
A30. A hot one for the press. ~ IRON
A31. If the Hoover delegates won't stand for it, this is what they can do. ~ SIT
A33. A ballot without a head. ~ ALLOT
A34. What the machine can do for the women. ~ SEW
A35. If this grabs at the presidential seat, we may get the nude deal. ~ DOG
A36. Hoover belongs to this White House organization. ~ ALUMNI
A37. Headquarters for both parties. ~ PILLOWS
A39. To pack again. ~ RELOAD
A43. This keeps asking "Who—Who?" ~ OWL
A44. Where to find Washington pie, roasted candy dates and political plums. ~ MENU
