A48. The opposing argument. ~ CON
A49. A Hindu farmer (sounds like a riot). ~ RYOT
A50. What a straw vote makes. ~ TEST
A51. A motion that was never finished. ~ MO
A52. This is one half. ~ SEMI
A53. The Dems. ~ INS
A54. Everybody's Uncle these days. ~ SAM
A55. This Johnny is a dark horse. ~ DOE
A58. The part of the radio that is in the studio. ~ DIO
A59. A bone to pick. ~ OS
A60. The chance a third party has. ~ SLIM
A61. New zeal for the winners. ~ ELAN
A63. Dublin the end of Dublin. ~ NN
A64. A grand thing that adds tone to the party. ~ PIANO
A65. The vision of the White House will be only this to some of the candidates. ~ MIRAGE
A67. A coming out party for presidential candidates. ~ CONVENTION
A68. One of Hoover's only supporters. ~ LEG

D1. The present cause of floods, tornadoes, dust storms and crack-ups (so they say). ~ ADMINISTRATION
D2. A special delivery to the convention. ~ LECTURE
D3. They can always make a place for this one. ~ PL
D4. This may be felt at the convention and probably talked thru. ~ HAT
D5. Favorable votes. ~ AYES
D6. This will be found in the parade of the states. ~ POMP
D7. Short weight. ~ LB
D8. We hope this will be bright for the future, whoever is elected. ~ ASPECT
D9. They have made a pile in this fabric. ~ TERRY
D10. The biggest kicker in the pool. ~ FROG
D11. This one is starting the ovations now. ~ OVA
D12. The Republican keynote. ~ RE
D15. Democratic football (ask any Republican). ~ CONSTITUTION
D18. This can go for half rate. ~ RA
D20. The man who beats, gets this. ~ BATON
D22. To pack. ~ STOW
D25. This gives a negative side to the picture. ~ FILM
D27. When the noes have it, this starts sneezing. ~ SN
D29. When the nose has it. this starts sneezing. ~ FLU
D31. A shining light that was spotted this year. ~ SOL
D32. The white house. ~ IGLOO
D33. Whose hat will be missing this year? ~ ALS
D35. This is often done. ~ DID
D36. It can fill any platform full of holes. ~ AWL
D37. How the conservatives will stand. ~ PAT
D38. What dictators would like to do to the world. ~ OWN
D40. What the committee does to make the platform on the level. ~ EVENS
D41. What the minority always gets. ~ LESS
D42. The last half of the report. ~ ORT
D44. Who rules the President? (abbr.) ~ MRS
D45. What the onlooker did. ~ EYED
D46. The hope of the party. ~ NOMINEE
D48. The people who do the voting. ~ COMMON
D51. As thou goest, US goes. ~ MAINE
D54. One of a European race. ~ SLAV
D55. The other half. ~ DEMI
D56. A mix-up. ~ OLIO
D57. What Hoover would like to do to the nomination. ~ EARN
D60. Committed by the wilder parties. ~ SIN
D62. A small part of North America. ~ NA
D64. An entry into politics. ~ PO
D66. All we get of the glory of it. ~ GL


